# Frontend learned rules

Auto-appended by agent when user states general pattern/constraint during chat.

- Always follow existing frontend structure. Before creating new: check if functionality exists, if it can be extended, and if it's readable. Never create new paths when existing patterns suffice.
- Follow UI/UX identity of existing pages. Match component patterns, styling conventions, layout structures, and user flow patterns.
- Keep frontend UX validation even when backend doesn't require it — user tracking/awareness features are valuable (e.g., expected count matching).
- Infer API endpoint structure from backend code (controllers, DTOs, services) instead of accessing swagger/web pages.
- Don't redesign or delete working code when backend doesn't support it yet — preserve for future use.
- Worktree isolation MANDATORY before any code edit. Before first edit: invoke `using-git-worktrees` skill → create branch from HEAD → create worktree → cd into worktree → install deps. If `using-git-worktrees` skill unavailable, manually execute steps per AGENTS.md Session Isolation section. Never edit code in main checkout.
- Always use pnpm (not npm) in the frontend repo. User override of AGENTS.md default.
- Design frontend components, hooks, and utilities to be reusable. If a pattern is likely to be used in multiple places, make it a general-purpose abstraction with well-defined props/parameters rather than a one-off.
- NO `any` in frontend code. Never annotate values/params with `any` (e.g. `(op: any)`, `(a: any)`, `as any`). Type against the real model (e.g. `OrderProduct`, `OrderProductAttribute`) instead. `catch (err: any)` is the only tolerated exception; narrow it with a typed guard when reading fields. Enforced 2026-07-19 after the variant refactor introduced `op: any` casts in 5 OrderCard consumers + 2 mapper helpers.
- Frontend types MUST mirror the actual backend response shape from the endpoint that produces the data. Derive shapes from backend DTOs (e.g. `OrderProductDto` in orders/orders.service.ts serializer) — do not invent fields the API does not send (e.g. `OrderProduct.quantity` is not in `OrderProductDto`; `customVariants`/`attributes` must match `PrismaJson.CustomVariants` / serializer output). Enforced 2026-07-19.
- Always store the design spec and implementation plan as repo docs (root repo `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md` and `docs/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md`) BEFORE starting implementation. Stated 2026-08-13.

